From: Codex <codex@local>
Subject: [PATCH] net: dsa: qca8k: skip QCA8386 MIB init in RAM trace build

The v12 RAM-only trace reaches qca8k_mib_init() after successfully reading
QCA8386 switch ID 0x17 and entering DSA setup.  The first MIB operation then
stops kernel/network progress before the next phase marker is emitted.

QCA8386 is not register-compatible with the older QCA8K MIB block at this
point in the bring-up.  Skip MIB initialization only for QCA8386 so the
diagnostic build can trace the remaining setup phases.  This is deliberately
not a production fix; statistics remain unavailable until the QCA8386 MIB
register layout and access sequence are implemented correctly.
---
--- a/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/dsa/qca/qca8k-8xxx.c
@@ -1995,10 +1995,15 @@ qca8k_setup(struct dsa_switch *ds)
 	}
 
 	dev_info(priv->dev, "trace setup: initialize MIB\n");
-	/* Enable MIB counters */
-	ret = qca8k_mib_init(priv);
-	if (ret)
-		dev_warn(priv->dev, "mib init failed");
+	if (priv->switch_id == QCA8K_ID_QCA8386) {
+		dev_warn(priv->dev,
+			 "trace setup: skip QCA8386 MIB init after v12 runtime hang\n");
+	} else {
+		/* Enable MIB counters */
+		ret = qca8k_mib_init(priv);
+		if (ret)
+			dev_warn(priv->dev, "mib init failed");
+	}
 
 	dev_info(priv->dev, "trace setup: clear forwarding membership\n");
 	/* Initial setup of all ports */
